Find $\tan Y$ in the right triangle shown below.

[asy]
pair X,Y,Z;
X = (0,0);
Y = (24,0);
Z = (0,7);
draw(X--Y--Z--X);
draw(rightanglemark(Y,X,Z,23));
label("$X$",X,SW);
label("$Y$",Y,SE);
label("$Z$",Z,N);
label("$25$",(Y+Z)/2,NE);
label("$24$",Y/2,S);
[/asy]

solution_steps:
In a right triangle, the tangent of an angle is the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the side adjacent to the angle.
In this triangle, $\tan Y = \frac{Z}{Y} = \frac{7}{24}$.
Therefore, $\tan Y = \boxed{\frac{7}{24}}$.The answer is: \frac{7}{24}

