Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl} x^2-4 & \text{ if }x < 7, \\
x-13 & \text{ if } x \geq 7.
\end{array}
\right.\] What is $f(f(f(17)))$?

solution_steps:
We can simplify the expression as follows:
$$\frac{2^{n+4} - 2(2^n)}{2(2^{n+3})} = \frac{2^n \cdot 2^4 - 2 \cdot 2^n}{2 \cdot 2^n \cdot 2^3} = \frac{16 \cdot 2^n - 2 \cdot 2^n}{2 \cdot 8 \cdot 2^n} = \frac{14 \cdot 2^n}{16 \cdot 2^n} = \frac{14}{16} = \boxed{\frac{7}{8}}.$$
The answer is: \frac{7}{8}

