First, we solve the equation $3x - 5 = 10x + 9$:
\begin{align*}
3x - 5 &= 10x + 9 \\
-7x &= 14 \\
x &= -2.
\end{align*}
Next, we substitute $x = -2$ into $4(x + 7)$:
\begin{align*}
4(-2 + 7) &= 4(5) \\
&= \boxed{20}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 20

