solution_steps:
Since $\sin$ has period $360^\circ$, we can subtract multiples of $360^\circ$ from $315^\circ$ to obtain an angle whose sine we can more easily find.
We have \[
\begin{aligned} 315^\circ &= 360^\circ - 45^\circ \\ &= -45^\circ.\end{aligned}
\]Since $\sin$ is an odd function, $\sin (-45^\circ) = -\sin 45^\circ = \boxed{-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}}.$
The answer is: -\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}

We can perform long division to find the remainder when $10x^3-7x^2+ax+6$ is divided by $2x^2-3x+1$:
\[
\begin{array}{c|cc(cc)}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{5x} & +1 \\
\cline{2-5}
2x^2-3x+1 & 10x^3 & -7x^2 & ax & +6 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{-10x^3} & +15x^2 & -5x \\
\cline{2-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & 8x^2 & (a-5)x & +6 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & -8x^2 & +12x & -4 \\
\cline{3-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & (a-5+12)x & +2 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & \multicolumn{1}{r}{} & (a+7)x & +2 \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & \multicolumn{1}{r}{} & 0 & (a+7)x & +2 \\
\end{array}
\]
In order for the remainder to be constant, the coefficient of $x$ in the remainder must be equal to 0.
Therefore, we have $(a+7)x + 2 = 0$, which implies $a+7=0$.
Thus, $a=\boxed{-7}$.The answer is: -7

