We are given that $abc = 64,$ which expands as $(b - d) b (b + d) = 64.$  This simplifies to $b^3 - d^2 b = 64.$

We want to minimize $b,$ so we maximize $d^2.$  Since $d^2$ is nonnegative, this means we should maximize $b.$

