2^1 &\equiv 2 \pmod{7} \\
2^2 &\equiv 4 \pmod{7} \\
2^3 &\equiv 1 \pmod{7} \\
2^4 &\equiv 2 \pmod{7}
\end{align*}
From the pattern, we see that $2^3 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}$ and $2^4 \equiv 2 \pmod{7}$, so we can conclude that $2^{87} \equiv 2^{3\cdot28+3} \equiv (2^3)^{28}\cdot 2^3 \equiv 1^{28}\cdot 2^3 \equiv 8 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}$.
Therefore, $2^{87} +3 \equiv 1+3 \equiv 4 \pmod{7}$.
The remainder when $2^{87} +3$ is divided by 7 is $\boxed{4}$.The answer is: 4

